  "notes": "COMMON PATTERNS:\n・{停電|ていでん}する (there is a power outage)\n・{停電|ていでん}になる (to become a blackout, for power to go out)\n・{停電|ていでん}が{復旧|ふっきゅう}する (power is restored)\n\nRELATED TERMS:\n・{計画|けいかく}{停電|ていでん} (planned power outage, rolling blackout)\n・{大規模|だいきぼ}{停電|ていでん} (large-scale blackout)\n・{復旧|ふっきゅう} (restoration, recovery)\n\nUSAGE NOTE:\nIn Japan, {計画|けいかく}{停電|ていでん} (planned power outages) were implemented after the 2011 earthquake to manage electricity shortages.",
